# Subagents

**Before non-trivial work** (research, implement, review, structure, multi-file
edits — not a typo or one-liner):

1. **Read** `pack-shared/subagents.md`

The main agent stays in its smart zone: decide, ask the user, dispatch **Task**
workers, and **review** their Completions. It does not do that labor itself.
Workers stay in theirs: one bounded job.

When surfaces, slices, or review axes are independent, launch **one Task per
lane in the same turn**. There is **no cap of two**. Sequential Tasks are
required when there is only one non-trivial job.

Pick any **listed** Task type that fits — pack roles (**explorer**,
**architect**, **implementer**, **reviewer**, **pr-reviewer**) or Cursor
built-ins (**explore**, **generalPurpose**, and others on the Task list). Do
not use reviewer for a GitHub PR, and do not use pr-reviewer for a local
branch.

Trivial work (typo, pure rename, git status, reading existing terminals) may
stay on the main agent. Never spawn verification-only MCP/lint ritual Tasks.

Worker **Read first** must include `taste/doctrine.md` and
`architecture/doctrine.md`.
